<title>JAPAN: Japan Nov M2+CD money supply up 3.3 pct yr/yr -- BOJ.</title>
<headline>Japan Nov M2+CD money supply up 3.3 pct yr/yr -- BOJ.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's broadly defined money supply average of M2 plus certificates of deposit (CDs) grew a preliminary 3.3 percent in November from a year earlier, the Bank of Japan (BOJ) said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>A breakdown of money supply figures follows:</p>
<p>(Year-on-year percentage changes)</p>
<p>			     NOV PRELIM  OCT REVISED SEPT</p>
<p> Unadjusted M2 + CDs    +3.3	  +3.7	 + 3.5</p>
<p>    M1		     +11.0	 +11.0	 +12.2</p>
<p>    CDs		    +56.2	 +57.7	 +25.5</p>
<p>			     NOV PRELIM  OCT REVISED SEPT</p>
<p> Broadest money measure+3.5	  +3.6	  +3.6</p>
<p>(Annualised month-on-month percentage changes)</p>
<p>			     NOV PRELIM  OCT REVISED SEPT</p>
<p> Adjusted M2 + CDs     +2.0	  +4.8	  +0.9</p>
<p>(Average outstanding yen levels)</p>
<p>				NOV PRELIM  OCT REVISED SEPT</p>
<p> Unadjusted M2+CDs     555.7 trln  555.6 trln 556.1 trln</p>
<p>    M1		     163.9 trln  161.8 trln 163.6 trln</p>
<p>    CDs		     16.3 trln   15.9 trln  13.6 trln</p>
<p>Broadest liquidity  1,125.3 trln1,123.0 trln1,121.9 trln</p>
</text>
